{"acronym":"STEP 10","arm_groups":[{"intervention_names":["Drug: Semaglutide 2.4 mg"],"label":"Semaglutide","type":"EXPERIMENTAL"},{"intervention_names":["Drug: Placebo"],"label":"Placebo (semaglutide)","type":"PLACEBO_COMPARATOR"}],"brief_summary":"This study looks at how well a new medicine, called semaglutide, works at helping people with obesity and prediabetes.\n\nThis study will look at how much weight participants lose, and if participants can go from having blood sugar that is higher than normal (prediabetes) to having normal blood sugar.\n\nSemaglutide is compared to a \"dummy\" medicine. The \"dummy\" medicine looks like semaglutide but has no effect on the body.\n\nIn addition to taking the medicine, participants will have talks with study staff about healthy food choices, how to be more physically active and what participants can do to lose weight.\n\nParticipants will either get semaglutide or \"dummy\" medicine - which treatment they get is decided by chance. Participants are 2 times as likely to get semaglutide as \"dummy\" medicine.\n\nParticipants will need to take 1 injection once a week. The study medicine is injected with a thin needle in a skin fold in the stomach, thigh or upper arm.\n\nThe study will last for about 19 months. Participants have to take the study medicine every week for the first 12 months. The last 7 months participants will not take any medication.\n\nParticipants will have 14 clinic visits and 1 phone call with the study staff. At 9 of the clinic visits Participants will have blood samples taken. Women cannot take part if pregnant, breast-feeding or plan to become pregnant during the study period.","brief_title":"Research Study Looking at How Well Semaglutide Works in People Living With Obesity and Prediabetes","collaborators":[],"completion_date":{"date":"2023-07-14","type":"ACTUAL"},"conditions":["Obesity"],"design":{"allocation":"RANDOMIZED","intervention_model":"PARALLEL","masking":"QUADRUPLE","primary_purpose":"TREATMENT","who_masked":["PARTICIPANT","CARE_PROVIDER","INVESTIGATOR","OUTCOMES_ASSESSOR"]},"eligibility":{"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Male or female aged greater than or equal to 18 years at the time of signing informed consent.\n* BMI greater than or equal to 30.0 kg/m\\^2\n* Prediabetes defined as at least one of the following:\n\n  * HbA1c between 6.0 and 6.4 percent (42 and 47 mmol/mol) (both inclusive) as measured by central laboratory at screening.\n  * FPG between 5.5 and 6.9 mmol/L (99 and 125 mg/dL) (both inclusive) as measured by central laboratory at screening.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* History of type 1 or type 2 diabetes.\n* Treatment with glucose-lowering agent(s) within 90 days before screening.\n* HbA1c greater than or equal to 6.5 percent (greater than or equal to 48 mmol/mol) as measured by central laboratory at screening.\n* FPG greater than or equal to 7.0mmol/L (126 mg/dL) as measured by central laboratory at screening.\n\nA self-reported change in body weight greater than 5 kg (11 lbs) within 90 days before screening irrespective of medical records.\n\n* Treatment with any medication for the indication of obesity within the past 90 days before screening.","healthy_volunteers":false,"maximum_age":null,"minimum_age":"18 Years","sex":"ALL","std_ages":["ADULT","OLDER_ADULT"]},"enrollment":{"count":207,"type":"ACTUAL"},"first_posted":"2021-09-10","has_results":true,"interventions":[{"name":"Semaglutide 2.4 mg","other_names":[],"type":"DRUG"},{"name":"Placebo","other_names":[],"type":"DRUG"}],"last_known_status":null,"last_update_posted":"2026-01-29","lead_sponsor":{"class":"INDUSTRY","name":"Novo Nordisk A/S"},"nct_id":"NCT05040971","official_title":"Efficacy and Safety of Subcutaneous Semaglutide 2.4 mg Once-weekly in Subjects With Obesity and Prediabetes","overall_status":"COMPLETED","phases":["PHASE3"],"primary_completion_date":{"date":"2023-01-06","type":"ACTUAL"},"primary_outcomes":[{"measure":"Change in Body Weight (Percentage [%])","time_frame":"From randomisation (week 0) to end of treatment (week 52)"},{"measure":"Participants With Change to Normoglycemia","time_frame":"At week 52"}],"results_first_posted":"2024-10-28","sites":[{"city":"Québec","country":"Canada","facility":"CHU de Quebec-Universite Laval","lat":46.81228,"lon":-71.21454,"state":null,"status":null},{"city":"Québec","country":"Canada","facility":"Institut universitaire de cardiologie","lat":46.81228,"lon":-71.21454,"state":null,"status":null},{"city":"Calgary","country":"Canada","facility":"C-endo Diab Endo Clin Calgery","lat":51.05011,"lon":-114.08529,"state":"Alberta","status":null},{"city":"Calgary","country":"Canada","facility":"LMC Clin Res Inc. Calgary","lat":51.05011,"lon":-114.08529,"state":"Alberta","status":null},{"city":"Calgary","country":"Canada","facility":"University of Calgary","lat":51.05011,"lon":-114.08529,"state":"Alberta","status":null},{"city":"Edmonton","country":"Canada","facility":"Weight Wise Clinic","lat":53.55014,"lon":-113.46871,"state":"Alberta","status":null},{"city":"Surrey","country":"Canada","facility":"Ocean West Research Clinic","lat":49.10635,"lon":-122.82509,"state":"British Columbia","status":null},{"city":"Moncton","country":"Canada","facility":"G.A. Research Associates Ltd.","lat":46.09454,"lon":-64.7965,"state":"New Brunswick","status":null},{"city":"Halifax","country":"Canada","facility":"Nova Scotia Hlth Halifax","lat":44.64269,"lon":-63.57688,"state":"Nova Scotia","status":null},{"city":"Barrie","country":"Canada","facility":"LMC Diabetes & Endocrinology (Barrie)","lat":44.40011,"lon":-79.66634,"state":"Ontario","status":null},{"city":"Brampton","country":"Canada","facility":"LMC ClinRsrh Inc.Brampton","lat":43.68341,"lon":-79.76633,"state":"Ontario","status":null},{"city":"Concord","country":"Canada","facility":"LMC Clin Res Inc. Thornhill","lat":43.80011,"lon":-79.48291,"state":"Ontario","status":null},{"city":"Etobicoke","country":"Canada","facility":"LMC Endo Ctr (Etobicoke) Ltd","lat"